<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  RE-DERIVED, not inherited (#1020 wave 3 lane F, D-1020-F7).

  v0's file grants five entitlements. Two of them are gone here and the reason
  for each is a property of this product rather than a tidy-up:

    * `com.apple.security.network.server` — REMOVED. That entitlement is what a
      LISTENING process needs, and #1020 rules that this product has none: the
      seat's only door is a Unix domain socket, and `cargo xtask gate`'s
      `no-listening-socket` rule holds the claim in code. Keeping it would have
      granted the app a capability nothing in it uses.
    * `com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation` — REMOVED. That is what
      loading an unsigned dylib into this process needs. The seat is a SEPARATE
      BINARY spawned as a child, not a library, so nothing unsigned is ever
      loaded here. (If a future build links the core as a dylib instead, this
      entitlement comes back with that change and not before.)

  The three that remain are Chromium's, not ours: V8 needs JIT and the
  writable-executable pages that go with it, and `network.client` is what the
  renderer's own fetches and iroh's UDP need.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
